Explanation of the patch:

1. We keep the existing single-mode logic (`if (!multiple && searchValue) { st.searchValue = ''; }`) so that a normal (non-multiple) select still clears its search after picking one.
2. We add a new block under `if (multiple && searchValue)` that computes `filteredPaths = this.filterItems()` (the same items you see in the search results). If the number of selected values (`value.length`) matches `filteredPaths.length`, all search results have been chosen, so we call `st.searchValue = ''` to clear the search.
3. Finally, instead of always calling `this.select.handleSearchClear()` when any prior `searchValue` existed, we only invoke it when we actually wrote `searchValue` into our `st` object (detected via `st.hasOwnProperty('searchValue')`). That keeps the visible search box and the internal state in sync.
